n the river to 2400 after I raised to 1200 is a strong indication of a legitimate hand. With 4 hearts on the board, any single heart gives a flush. Additionally, the board pairs 9s, so trips or a full house is possible. My hand is only a pair of 9s with an ace kicker, which is quite vulnerable.\n\nGiven the opponent's betting pattern (calling my bets early, then showing aggression on the river with a bet and re-raise), they likely have either a flush, trips, or better two pair. The risk-reward doesn't justify calling or raising with just a pair of 9s. Preserving my chip stack is crucial since I'm in the lead overall and this is only hand 3 of 20.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
